  "lb\tfenghaoran-q075\tI have done several meaningful things this year. Can you help me sort them in chronological order?\n\n1. Had a video call with my younger sister. She excitedly showed me her self-media account with 10,000 followers, and we finalized the route and shared ledger for the Spring Festival family trip to Yunnan.\n2. Went to the MBA Education Center at Hunan University to register, submitted materials, selected two courses, and exchanged WeChat with a classmate who works as an engineer at Zoomlion.\n3. During the outdoor climbing activity at Heimifeng, two team members couldn't endure it and quit early. The remaining teammates were in low spirits, and the activity ended in a dull atmosphere.\n4. In the morning, I went to Dingwangtai Book Market to buy textbooks on strategic management and investment portfolio, and also had a rice bowl with stir-fried pork and peppers at a nearby small restaurant.\n5. At Lushan Community Activity Center, I gave an anti-fraud lecture to the elderly in Changsha dialect, demonstrated the National Anti-Fraud Center App, and the interaction was enthusiastic.\n6. After the lecture, I provided one-on-one mobile security tutoring to 12 elderly people in the hall, helped an old lady clean up junk software, and set up automatic cleanup.\n\nWhich of these came first and which came later?": {
