  "lb\tfenghaoran-q095\tI experienced several memorable things this year. Can you help me put them in chronological order?\n1. I unboxed a new camera in my study, set the parameters, took a photo, and sent it to a photography buddy.\n2. I arrived at the physical examination center at the scheduled time (that day I took a taxi to the hospital and checked my account balance on the way). After verifying my identity at the front desk and receiving the examination form, I completed blood draw (complete blood count, liver and kidney function, lipid panel), abdominal ultrasound, electrocardiogram, chest X-ray, and urine test in sequence. The whole process took about 1.5 hours and was smooth and efficient. After the examination, I felt my stomach was empty and urgently needed energy, so I went to Zhougong Zhoupou opposite the hospital for breakfast.\n3. In the second half of the outdoor climbing, some team members withdrew, the activity ended early, and the atmosphere was dull.\n4. I returned to the hospital's physical examination center (that morning I had eaten preserved egg and lean pork congee at Zhougong Zhoupou), collected some reports that were available immediately (such as complete blood count and urine routine), and went into Dr. Wang's office to listen to the interpretation. Dr. Wang pointed at the lipid report and seriously stated that total cholesterol and low-density lipoprotein were both slightly above normal, diagnosing mild hyperlipidemia, and recommending reducing high-fat diet, increasing aerobic exercise, and monitoring weight. Although I felt that being young was not a big deal, the doctor's authoritative advice and the records on 'Boohee Health' made me start to take it seriously.\n5. On the way back from climbing, I was persuaded by the coach, and after returning home, I apologized in the group.\n\nWhich of these happened first, and which happened later?": {
